  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "initialize_context_decompression",
    "file": "c-blosc2/blosc/blosc2.c",
    "description": "When processing a dictionary-bearing chunk, this function frees an existing `context->dict_ddict` at lines 2070-2072 but does not clear the pointer. It then validates the new dictionary metadata and can return early at lines 2075-2088 before assigning a replacement at line 2093. The context consequently retains a dangling non-NULL `dict_ddict`; later `blosc2_schunk_free` calls `blosc2_free_ctx`, which passes that stale pointer to `ZSTD_freeDDict` again, causing the reported heap-use-after-free/double-free behavior. The root fix is to clear the pointer immediately after freeing it, or validate/create the replacement before destroying the old dictionary.",
    "conditions": "The attacker-controlled frame must contain at least two chunks that are decompressed using the same super-chunk decompression context. An earlier chunk with `BLOSC2_USEDICT` must contain a sufficiently valid dictionary so `ZSTD_createDDict` stores a non-NULL `context->dict_ddict`. A later chunk must also set `BLOSC2_USEDICT`, causing the old dictionary to be freed, but must have malformed/truncated dictionary metadata\u2014fewer than 4 bytes for the size, an invalid size, or fewer dictionary bytes than the declared size\u2014so initialization returns before replacing the pointer. The fuzzer then exits its decompression loop and frees the super-chunk/context, triggering the second `ZSTD_freeDDict` on the stale pointer in `blosc2_free_ctx`."
  },
